{"text": " Your plan only works on good days. Most plans assume you'll have energy, time, and a good mood every single day. Then when bad day comes, you skip, and the whole thing quietly falls apart. So plan the bad day in advance. Give every habit two versions the full one and a smaller one for the days that go wrong. Training for a 5K, the full version is your 30-minute run. The bad day version is an easy 15-minute walk. Studying for an exam, the full version is two hours of practice questions. The bad day version is 15 minutes reviewing your notes. The rule is simple, on a bad day you don't skip, you switch. Because a streak isn't about doing everything every day, it's about never letting one bad day turn into a bad week. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.12, "text": " Your plan only works on good days. Most plans assume you'll have energy, time, and a good mood", "tokens": [50363, 3406, 1410, 691, 2499, 319, 922, 1528, 13, 4042, 3352, 7048, 345, 1183, 423, 2568, 11, 640, 11, 290, 257, 922, 10038, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0691333124714513, "compression_ratio": 1.723021582733813, "no_speech_prob": 0.0005833270843140781, "words": [{"word": " Your", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9336823225021362}, {"word": " plan", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.64, "probability": 0.9774911403656006}, {"word": " only", "start": 0.64, "end": 0.98, "probability": 0.9770129919052124}, {"word": " works", "start": 0.98, "end": 1.28, "probability": 0.9983810186386108}, {"word": " on", "start": 1.28, "end": 1.5, "probability": 0.9974683523178101}, {"word": " good", "start": 1.5, "end": 1.68, "probability": 0.9791279435157776}, {"word": " days.", "start": 1.68, "end": 2.0, "probability": 0.9980617165565491}, {"word": " Most", "start": 2.6, "end": 2